<p>A recent review of empirical work indicates that argument mapping enhances critical thinking skills (Nesbit &amp; Liu, 2025), and although argument mapping programs may not be necessary to achieve notable critical thinking gains (Harrell, 2008), the use of such tools appears to enhance the effectiveness of argument mapping instruction (Eftekhari et al., 2016). From a teaching perspective, the authors can testify to four notable benefits to incorporating an argument mapping program into their course: mapping online is significantly faster than mapping on a whiteboard, maps projected onto a screen are easier for students to see, maps created using an online mapping tool can be easily retrieved for development or discussion over multiple class periods, and computer-based mapping can make feedback provision more efficient.</p>
<p>Readers who have questions about Argumentation.io or Because, or who would like to explore ways to include argument mapping in their classes, are warmly welcome to reach out to the authors.</p>
